::CW_U04_L03_GP_Q01::Poem: The suitcase waited by the door, still wearing its paper tag. What implied meaning is best supported?{
~A. The poem is only about luggage prices.#Incorrect. The suitcase is an object, but the details suggest more than cost.
~C. The poem proves the speaker hates travel.#Incorrect. Hate is not supported by the evidence.
=
~D. The suitcase is definitely alive.#Incorrect. Waited is figurative, not literal life.
}

::CW_U04_L03_GP_Q02::Poem: She left one window open after the argument. Which interpretation is most reasonable?{
=
~B. The line only teaches home safety.#Incorrect. A poem can use a window symbolically.
~C. The window proves the argument is solved.#Incorrect. The poem does not prove complete resolution.
~D. The speaker wants bad weather.#Incorrect. Weather is not mentioned.
}

::CW_U04_L03_GP_Q03::Poem: The clock stopped at three, but the house kept listening. What creates ambiguity?{
~A. The exact color of the clock is missing.#Incorrect. Missing color is not the central ambiguity.
=
~C. The word house is too difficult.#Incorrect. The word is clear.
~D. The poem has no implied meaning.#Incorrect. The details suggest more beneath the literal scene.
}

::CW_U04_L03_GP_Q04::Poem: I planted the letter beneath the rosebush. Which layered meaning is strongest?{
~A. The speaker is only gardening.#Incorrect. A letter being planted suggests symbolic action.
~C. The rosebush is definitely poisonous.#Incorrect. No evidence supports poison.
~D. The letter is a seed packet.#Incorrect. The poem says letter, not seed packet.
=
}

::CW_U04_L03_GP_Q05::Poem: The bridge disappeared in fog, but my feet kept moving. What does the image most likely suggest?{
~A. The speaker can see everything clearly.#Incorrect. Fog suggests uncertainty.
~B. The bridge is poorly built.#Incorrect. The focus is symbolic movement, not construction.
=
~D. The poem is about weather only.#Incorrect. Weather supports the deeper meaning.
}
